  "id": "Southwark-26_AP_0814",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "T1 Fraxinus excelsior (Ash) - Felling to Ground Level\rCarry out the removal of the Fraxinus excelsior by felling to ground level. The tree is exhibiting multiple fungal fruiting bodies, indicating decay within the structure. Works shall be undertaken carefully to manage any compromised timber and ensure safe removal without damage to surrounding areas.\rT2 Tilia spp. (Lime) - Crown Reduction and Epicormic Removal\rCarry out a crown reduction of the Tilia by approximately 2.5 metres in height. Works shall include the removal of epicormic growth from the main stem and lower crown. Branches shall be selectively shortened to suitable secondary growth points to maintain a balanced and natural canopy structure.\rT3 Aesculus hippocastanum (Large Horse Chestnut) - Crown Reduction\rCarry out a crown reduction of the large Aesculus hippocastanum by approximately 2.5 metres in height and 1.5 metres in lateral spread. Works shall comprise selectively shortening branches to suitable secondary growth points to reduce canopy size whilst maintaining structural integrity and a balanced crown.\rT4 Aesculus hippocastanum (Horse Chestnut) - Crown Reduction\rCarry out a crown reduction of the Aesculus hippocastanum by approximately 2.5 metres in height and 1.5 metres in lateral spread. Works shall involve selectively shortening branch lengths to suitable pruning points to maintain a natural form and balanced canopy",
